{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":3058373,"ns":0,"title":"Atom (measure theory)","extract":"In mathematics, more precisely in measure theory, an atom is a measurable set that has positive measure and contains no set of smaller positive measures. A measure that has no atoms is called non-atomic or atomless.","description":"Minimal measurable set with positive measure","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}